                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hate to be that guy after being excited for this game, but I do not recommend this\n\nFirst off its very short for the price. The first playthrough was an hour and a half for me. You have the option to play again as someone else but I didn't \n\nSecondly the AI is awful. Enemies will just stare you in the face they don't react to to and will keep running their cycle. You have to chase down bosses and when they are done attacking will just stand there for a good 5 seconds. There was no challenge or fun in fighting so to me it loses any replay value\n\nA small thing I would like to see fixed is the lack of animations when you shoot a long distance spell, they just fire out of your body standing perfectly still and it looks silly\n\nAlso I don't know if it's a bug but when you fire spells your synch with your spirit goes up whether you're hitting anything or not so you can just charge the synch on all spirits easily before a boss.\n\nI feel like this game had potential but really fell short\n\n\n",
